From cca19c65133ed279469d0c719a566d1b7dad4d46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guilhem Bichot <guilhem.bichot@contributor>


Date: Wed, 12 Mar 2025 11:16:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BUGFIX

Fix for a bug: range optimizer scanning too many index cells in TPC-C

select * from t1, t2 where t1.a=100 and t2.a>=t1.b-20 and t2.a<t1.b;

(see the added test) we have a constant table t1 and a range condition
on t2 involving values from t1.

The bug's symptom was that the range scan was set up as:
 -> Covering index range scan on t2 using a over (NULL < a < 100)

So it was lacking the left bound (80). Even though the upper filter
made sure to test t2.a>80, thus the result was correct, it means the
entire range (-inf,100) was scanned by the access method. Which is a
waste, and made a big speed difference in transaction "stocklevel" of
some variant of TPC-C (BenchmarkSQL). After fixing, it goes from 140k
tpmc to 730k.

Here is the problem's cause. After discovering that t1 is constant, we
update the sargables (used by the range optimizer) by checking if
their right-hand side is now constant. We properly saw that in the
sargable t2.a<t1.b the right side is constant, but missed that in the
sargable t2.a>=t1.b-20 the right side is also constant: this is
because the_minus_item->const_item() is now out of date.

The fix is to refresh this value. After that we get:
 -> Covering index range scan on t2 using a over (80 <= a < 100)

For reference: the tpc-c query:

explain format=tree
SELECT count(*) AS low_stock FROM (
  SELECT s_w_id, s_i_id, s_quantity FROM stock1
  WHERE s_w_id = '23' AND s_quantity < '18' AND s_i_id IN (
    SELECT ol_i_id FROM district1 JOIN order_line1 ON
    ol_w_id = d_w_id AND ol_d_id = d_id AND ol_o_id >= d_next_o_id - 20 AND ol_o_id < d_next_o_id
    WHERE d_w_id = '23' AND d_id = '3' )
) AS L;

Original plan:

 -> Aggregate: count(0)  (cost=75545 rows=1)
    -> Remove duplicate stock1 rows using temporary table (weedout)  (cost=73659 rows=18865)
        -> Nested loop inner join  (cost=73659 rows=18865)
            -> Filter: ((order_line1.ol_d_id = '3') and (order_line1.ol_w_id = '23') and (order_line1.ol_o_id >= <cache>(('3001' - 20))) and (order_line1.ol_o_id < '3001') and (order_line1.ol_i_id is not null))  (cost=11399 rows=56602)
                -> Index range scan on order_line1 using PRIMARY over (ol_w_id = 23 AND ol_d_id = 3 AND ol_o_id < 3001)  (cost=11399 rows=56602)
            -> Filter: (stock1.s_quantity < 18)  (cost=1 rows=0.333)
                -> Single-row index lookup on stock1 using PRIMARY (s_w_id=23, s_i_id=order_line1.ol_i_id)  (cost=1 rows=1)

After the fix (notice the cost&rows numbers decrease):
                -> Index range scan on order_line1 using PRIMARY over (ol_w_id = 23 AND ol_d_id = 3 AND 2981 <= ol_o_id < 3001)  (cost=43.1 rows=209)

